    "result": "Perfect! My implementation is complete and follows all project rules. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\nI've successfully added the `--threshold` feature to `frai eval` that allows gating CI jobs on metric scores. The implementation consists of:\n\n### **Modified Files:**\n\n1. **`packages/frai-core/src/eval/index.js`** - Core logic\n   - Enhanced `generateReport` to accept optional `thresholds` parameter\n   - Implements threshold validation (metrics with null scores fail)\n   - Adds `passed` and `thresholds` fields to reports when thresholds are provided\n   - Maintains backward compatibility (no fields added when no thresholds)\n\n2. **`packages/frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js`** - Report formatting\n   - Updated Markdown reporter to include \"Thresholds\" section with PASS/FAIL status\n   - JSON format naturally includes the threshold data\n\n3. **`packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts`** - CLI interface\n   - Added `threshold?: string[]` to `EvalOptions` interface\n   - Implemented `parseThresholds()` function with validation\n   - Implemented `validateThresholds()` function to check metric IDs\n   - Updated `runEvalCommand()` to orchestrate the flow\n   - Added `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option (supports multiple uses)\n   - Proper exit codes: 0 (success), 1 (threshold failure), 2 (usage error)\n\n### **Features:**\n\n\u2705 **Threshold Format:** `--threshold exact_match=0.9` (can be used multiple times)  \n\u2705 **Validation:** Metric ID and value validation with helpful error messages  \n\u2705 **Null Score Handling:** Metrics with no score (e.g., exact_match without references) fail their threshold  \n\u2705 **Report Integration:** Both JSON and Markdown formats include threshold results  \n\u2705 **Custom Metrics:** Works with custom metrics passed to `runEvaluations`  \n\u2705 **Exit Codes:** Proper error codes for CI/CD integration  \n\u2705 **Backward Compatible:** Reports without thresholds unchanged  \n\u2705 